    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "07dc956e9fa4cf93625341063b13f80b2ea254dfdb2bff26cfda8121e1b7343b",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261107-0a822c5ae0173752",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "In the morning, drive about 30 minutes to the statue of the Virgin at roughly 4,000 m above sea level. The trail to the mountain refuge starts here. The ascent takes about 2 hours, and the return takes about 1 hour.\n\nThe trail crosses marshy highlands and a small Polylepis forest, with views of the valley along the way.\n\nIf you wish, you can continue from the refuge to the 5,116 m summit of Iliniza Norte. This adds approximately 2 hours of uphill hiking. It makes for a longer day, so the decision depends on how participants are feeling and on mountain conditions. The descent from the summit to the statue of the Virgin takes about 2 hours.\n\n**Accommodation:** Chuquiragua Lodge.  \n**Meals:** Breakfast, packed lunch and dinner."
    },
